  "slug": "presence-topic-a9d0",
  "summary": "Predicted structures and structure-aware embeddings are now used as direct readouts for missense variant effects and interaction-site prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is predicted structure or structure-aware representations used as constraints or features for biological prediction. UshEffect-3D, a gene-specific machine-learning predictor for USH2A missense variants, reclassifies 981 of 2,639 ClinVar VUS as likely pathogenic. SPPIDER-seq predicts partner-aware protein-protein interaction sites from ESM-2 embeddings with cross-attention, reaching AUROC up to 0.797. AlphaFold2 Evoformer latents are evaluated as features for calpain cleavage and nucleic-acid-binding site prediction, and AF2 is found more accurate than OpenFold3 on 271 protein-peptide complexes, with evidence of memorization. SNAC-DB adds structural diversity to antibody and VHH-antigen complex data, with 31-37% more diversity than SAbDab. What is new is predicted structure serving as a direct readout for variant effect in a single disease gene. Remaining items, on DNA-synthesis hazard screening, antimicrobial peptide benchmarking, and DDA proteomics, share the benchmarking framing rather than the structural focus.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-30"
}
